=== trackers, in full (reads GitHub)
$ sh <skills>/trackers/scripts/tracker-read.sh --url https://example.com/page
    tracker-read.sh: not a tracker link: example.com/page
    [exit 3]
    first line: # interactive pr list
$ sh <skills>/trackers/scripts/context-add-ticket.sh --effort <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed --url https://github.com/cli/cli/issues/1
    <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed/context/draft/docs/ticket-github.com-cli-cli-issues-1.md
    [exit 0]
=== context: the grill is no entry; the cut on the human's "done"
$ sh <skills>/crucible-context/scripts/context-add.sh --effort <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed --path <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed/events/000004-grill.ended.json --why the grill on what to fetch
    context-add.sh: --path <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed/events/000004-grill.ended.json is inside the effort's own folder: its facts reach the agents through the sender, never as a reference
    [exit 2]
$ sh <skills>/crucible-context/scripts/context-status.sh --effort <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed
    VERSION: none
    PENDING: yes
    [exit 0]
$ sh <skills>/crucible-context/scripts/context-cut.sh --effort <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed
    CONTEXT_FILE: <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed/events/000007-context.cut.json
    CONTEXT_SHA256: <hex>
    [exit 0]
=== spec, from the cut context and the grill, sealed in place
$ sh <skills>/crucible-spec/scripts/spec-approve.sh --effort <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed --draft <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed/spec/1.md
    <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed/events/000009-spec.approved.json
    [exit 0]
    v1 holds: diff-33d01e0.patch
    v1 holds: ticket-github.com-cli-cli-issues-1.md
$ sh <skills>/crucible-context/scripts/context-verify.sh --effort <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed --file <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed/events/000007-context.cut.json
    CONTEXT_FILE: <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed/events/000007-context.cut.json
    CONTEXT_SHA256: <hex>
    [exit 0]
=== effort-close sees a domain neighbour's open work
$ sh <skills>/crucible-effort/scripts/effort-close.sh --effort <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed --outcome done --words done
    effort-close.sh: open work: flow 3 "Know the work"; probe 1 "left running"; end it first, or close with --leave-open on the human's word
    [exit 2]
$ sh <skills>/crucible-dynamic-flow/scripts/flow-end.sh --flow <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed:3 --outcome done --evidence The human says so
    <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed/events/000010-flow.ended.json
    [exit 0]
$ sh <skills>/crucible-effort/scripts/effort-close.sh --effort <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed --outcome done --words done
    <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed/events/000011-effort.closed.json
    [exit 0]
$ sh <skills>/crucible-effort/scripts/effort-status.sh --effort <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed
    installed · closed, done, <at>: done
    [exit 0]
=== a domain script where core isn't beside it: refused plainly
$ sh <S>/lonely/trackers/scripts/context-add-ticket.sh --effort <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed --url https://github.com/cli/cli/issues/1
    context-add-ticket.sh: core's context isn't beside this skill (expected <S>/lonely/crucible-context); install first
    [exit 2]
$ sh <R>/domains/software-development/core/main-thread/code-context/scripts/context-add-commit.sh --effort <S>/space/efforts/<id>-installed --repo <S>/repo --ref HEAD
    context-add-commit.sh: core's context isn't beside this skill (expected <R>/domains/software-development/core/main-thread/crucible-context); install first
    [exit 2]
